NotesString/You can open this notes window for any project by selecting View->Notes...

This example shows the CAN interpreter displaying data from multiple frames.

There were 36 separate CAN data frames. You can use the menu function 
"View->Zoom All" to zoom out and see the entire CAN data sequence which 
took more than 11 seconds to complete. 

Using its hardware sample compression, the LogicPort had no trouble capturing 
595 megasamples of data in a single acquisition while sampling at a modest 50MHz.
Most logic analyzers without sample compression (even those with "deep memory")
would have run out of buffer space long before this sequence was completed.

This example also demonstrates how multiple instances of the interpreter allow you 
to display the raw data along with interpreted CAN data and bit-stuffing.

You can quickly zoom in or out by pressing the <+> or <-> keys on the numerical 
keypad of your keyboard. Press T on your keyboard to quickly scroll to the trigger 
position.

Please note that all of the example files are "read only" so that they remain intact
for future reference. You can change settings in these files for learning purposes, 
but the changes cannot be saved. You can however use the "Save As" option to 
save an editable copy of any example file.
/
